  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "When the base of a triangle is increased \\(10\\%\\) and the altitude to this base is decreased \\(10\\%,\\) the change in area is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\%\\) increase",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac12\\%\\) increase",
    "C": "\\(0\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac12\\%\\) decrease",
    "E": "\\(1\\%\\) decrease"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Let the original base and corresponding altitude be \\(b,h>0\\), so the original area is \\(K=\\tfrac12bh\\). Increasing the base by \\(10\\%\\) multiplies it by \\(1.10\\), while decreasing the altitude by \\(10\\%\\) multiplies it by \\(0.90\\). The new area is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac12(1.10b)(0.90h)\n=0.99\\left(\\frac12bh\\right)\n=0.99K.\n\\]\nThe area becomes \\(99\\%\\) of its original value, a \\(\\boxed{1\\%\\text{ decrease}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm E\\).",
